# The annotations of $FF63-$FF86 as TZX blocks 12 and 14 load them over the loader's end: the source of
# src/loader/tail.asm (../../kit/mkgame.py --part src/loader/tail.json). Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md.
# Witness: c1 (work/stage1/rec/c1): block 12 loaded at frame ~6200, block 14 at ~9800; LoadEnd ran at 11632.

@module tail ; The loader's new end: start the game through Mover
@about Block 12 (row 6 of BlockTable) writes $FF63-$FF79: the same start as LoaderStart's original tail but JP $A000. Block 14 (row 8) writes $FF7A-$FF86: the end that runs after the check byte, which jumps to Mover at $5B00 (block 15) when the XOR of the stream is 0.

$FF63 c TailStart ; LoadFailed set: Crash; else IY = $5C3A, IM 1, HL' = $2758, R = 0, JP $A000
> Reached when LoadBlock returns after the last block (the return address LoadBlock left). The JP $A000 enters the decoy area block 5 filled; in c1 the game never got here: LoadEnd's JP $5B00 comes first (c1 frame 11632).
$FF7A c TailEnd ; Border black; H (the XOR of the stream) 0: JP Mover ($5B00), else JP $0000
> POP DE drops $FF7B (LoadBlock's push); XOR A / OUT ($FE) black border; LD A,H / CP 1 / JP C,$5B00 when H = 0, JP $0000 (a reset) otherwise.
> Witness: L1 2 (c1).
